A||N||3||cscougar||Fuel pump fuse blows||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||08-02-2001||11:49 PM||||My son's 85 2m6 has a problem.  It runs fine without the air conditioner on.  When he turns on the a/c he can drive it 3 or 4 miles and then it blows the fuel pump/oil pressure switch fuse.  <P>We have replaced the fuel pump and the oil pressure switch.  The a/c is charged and is working very nice.  The oil pressure shows to be around 40-60 lbs.  <P>Any ideas....what causes this fuse to blow.<P>Thanks<P>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||08-03-2001||12:28 AM||||My guess would be that you have frayed wiring. The fuel pump relay and AC clutch relay are right next to each other on the fire wall. Check the wires going to these relays to see if they are rubbing on anything. They are located on the left hand side of the firewall (between the engine and driver) below the deck hinge.||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||08-03-2001||12:29 AM||||That's a strange one. I can't think of anywhere these three items have a shared circuit. Get my gm book tomorrow & look some more. Where is China Spring,Tex?||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-05-2001||01:26 PM||||They don't share any elecrtical circuits but they do share physical paths. Sounds allot like the 2 are pinched/melted together someplace. You'll have to physically inspect everything.||||reg||1
